&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve problems, not tickets.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll be handed a problem, usually described by the people living with it rather than specified in advance, and you&#39;ll own the design as well as the delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make admin work for the people who use it.&lt;/strong&gt; Staff should be able to see what a customer has bought, how they&#39;re billed and what limits they have, make a change, and trust the result, without needing to understand our internal models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across the company.&lt;/strong&gt; Finance, Customer Success, Support and Engineering are all your users. You&#39;ll learn their processes well enough to question a requirement rather than just build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion AI-assisted development.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll use LLMs and AI tools for planning, spikes, code and docs to accelerate velocity, while owning correctness and architectural quality yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the systems explain themselves.&lt;/strong&gt; Why a customer has the limits they have, and what produced an invoice, should be answerable without an engineer digging through code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the testing bar.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll decide what good looks like where mistakes cost money, build the harness to match, and hold the line on production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to talk if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in large, established codebases, and the judgement to tell when a system should be extended, reworked, or replaced outright, including the confidence to say so unprompted. Ruby on Rails will help you get to grips with what we have today, though we care more about your range than any one language, and what you build here may well not be Rails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of shaping architecture inside a system you inherited, including the data ownership decisions that come with drawing a boundary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to self-start, work through ambiguity, and make good decisions without a lot of hand-holding. We&#39;ll bring you problems, not designs, and we&#39;d expect you to push back when the answer is to change a process rather than write code.&lt;/li&gt;
